                                                                                "title":  "Santoli: The S\u0026P 500 is within striking distance of record as bull relies on familiar leadership",
                                                                                "source":  "Mike Santoli (CNBC)",
                                                                                "author":  "Michael Santoli",
                                                                                "url":  "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/22/santoli-the-sp-500-is-within-striking-distance-of-record-as-bull-relies-on-familiar-leadership.html",
                                                                                "date":  "2026-09-22",
                                                                                "imageUrl":  null,
                                                                                "summary":  "Santoli observes that months of \u0027bend-don\u0027t-break\u0027 market action have kept the S\u0026P 500 within reach of record highs despite persistent headwinds in rate-sensitive and consumer-facing sectors. Consumer cyclicals, industrials, and banks absorbed pressure from higher oil prices, elevated yields, and signs of household fatigue, while semiconductor stocks and mega-cap tech worked through AI-overspending concerns. The recovery has been narrow, concentrating in the same familiar large-cap tech leaders that drove previous legs of the bull market.",
                                                                                "take":  "Narrow leadership is a double-edged signal: it shows the bull has staying power, but it also means index returns are masking broad deterioration underneath. Investors benchmarked to the S\u0026P 500 may feel comfortable while their non-mega-cap holdings quietly underperform. The practical implication is to be deliberate about where breadth is or is not recovering ÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Â if semis and mid-cap tech begin to participate alongside mega-caps, that would be a genuine broadening signal worth adding risk into. Until then, the index level flatters the underlying health of the market, and active sector management matters more than it has in recent years.",
                                                                                "isNew":  true
